<title>USA: Palmer Wireless to buy back 600,000 common.</title>
<headline>Palmer Wireless to buy back 600,000 common.</headline>
<dateline>FT. MYERS, Fla. 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Palmer Wireless Inc said Friday that its board authorized a buyback of up to 600,000 shares of the company's class A common over the next 12 months.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that current market conditions do not reflect the long-term value of the company and therefore we will seek opportunities to repurchase our stock at attractive levels,&quot; the company stated.</p>
<p>Palmer Wireless owns and operates 17 non-wireline cellular telephone systems in Florida, Alabama, Georgia and South Carolina.</p>
</text>
